          "citation": "489 U.S. 189 (1989)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of the United States",
          "year": 1989,
          "date_decided": "1989-02-22",
          "holding": "The Supreme Court held that the Due Process Clause imposes no affirmative obligation on a State to protect a child from violence by a private actor, even where the agency knew of the danger, absent a custodial relationship that limits the child's freedom to act on his own behalf.",
          "relevance": "Because constitutional damages liability is foreclosed in most non-custodial cases, fatality review and legislative reform are the principal accountability mechanisms.",
          "quote": "But nothing in the language of the Due Process Clause itself requires the State to protect the life, liberty, and property of its citizens against invasion by private actors.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/112202/deshaney-v-winnebago-county-department-of-social-services/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 112202
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Doe ex rel. Johnson v. South Carolina Department of Social Services",
          "citation": "597 F.3d 163 (4th Cir. 2010)",
          "court": "United States Court of Appeals for the Fourth Circuit",
          "year": 2010,
          "date_decided": "2010-03-05",
          "holding": "The Fourth Circuit recognized that a child involuntarily removed from her home has a substantive due process right not to be placed in a known, dangerous foster care environment in deliberate indifference to her safety, but held the caseworker entitled to qualified immunity because that right was not clearly established at the time.",
          "relevance": "",
          "quote": "had a corresponding duty to refrain from placing her in a known, dangerous environment in deliberate indifference to her right to personal safety and security",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/1031686/doe-ex-rel-johnson-v-south-carolina-department-of-social-services/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 1031686
